Assuming you might have a boot image on a hard drive, try these:

>>> B DKA100
or
>>> B DKA200
and see if something starts up

Being RZ23s, you might have a very old stripped down copy of VMS, or
some type of unix system on it.  the other possibility is that there was
originally a DKA0 drive with the OS on it, but someone removed it.
