My admittedly vague recollection is that block I/O also gives you some
block-level shared-update interlocking support that QIO may not - and in
RMS-11 the additional (execution) overhead of going through RMS using block
I/O was fairly small (though I seem to remember hearing someone say recently
that the same may not be true of VMS/RMS).  And the RMS interface may be at
least somewhat more familiar to the people who wish RMS provided 32-bit VAR
record size support than QIO.

