David,

You've made some reasonable points, to be sure.  The proliferation of
cheap hardware is a factor here.

But why does the Windows registry grow and grow and grow?  Then it
becomes corrupted and you have to start all over again reloading
Windows?  Where are decent tools to manage the registry, to get rid of
all the crap that accumulates in it, and to un-corrupt it?  Nope,
