> for about $700 each.

My 2 cents:

I started with Redhat Linux 5.n around Easter time. I quickly discovered
that there were many megabytes of fixes and enhancements to download.
Far more than I was going to attempt to download at home, so I bought
Redhat 6.0. No sooner installed than I start to find yet more megabytes
of assorted fixes and enhancements to download, and that's just the
stuff I think I need!

Now I understand that 6.1 is out, but what am I getting into if I buy
that? More of the same? Two to three upgrades in less than a year? It's
getting worse than the M$ upgrade loop!

I have reached the stage where I just want a stable platform, and am
seriously considering the alternatives such as FreeBSD.

If and when I manage to get hold of a sensibly priced Alpha to run
Hobbyist VMS at home, I imagine I'd use the Intel box just for the stuff 
(such as Applixware) which doesn't run on VMS.

