In article <uYT84.67$4c.254573@news.optonline.net>, "Frank Sapienza" <sapienza@noesys.com> writes:
:In a cluster using DSSI for the interconnect, if there are two shared DSSI
:buses, does SCS use only one or both buses for cluster communications?  

  All paths will be configured, and the particular path chosen for each
  SCS circuit to the particular target node will be used until a trigger 
  (overload, path failure, higher class path availability, etc) warrants 
  the use of another.  As each SCS circuit is initiated, some basic load 
  balancing takes place (when multiple SCS paths in the same load class 
  exist to the target), and rebalancing occurs if/when a faster load 
  class path becomes available or when problem(s) with the chosen path(es)
  arise.  (Also -- on OpenVMS VAX only -- periodic SCS virtual circuit 
  rebalancing occurs when multiple paths exist in the same load class.
  OpenVMS Alpha does not currently support dynamic SCS balancing...)

:If it uses only one of them, how does it select which one to use?

  All paths will be configured.  That said, the choice of the path used
  for each circuit isn't necessarily particularly (externally obviously) 
  deterministic, and the only means available to control it is involves 
  the brute-force "bus" tools -- starting or stopping the entire SCS path.
  (And starting up an SCS path of the same load class doesn't necessarily 
  trigger rebalancing on OpenVMS Alpha...)

  As cluster interconnects are concerned, DSSI is in the same load class 
  as CI, but is rather less than CI in terms of actual throughput...  The
  network interconnects comprise the other (lesser) major SCS load class.
  NB: In some configurations, shared-access DSSI is (obviously) available 
  as a cluster (and storage) interconnect, and in other configurations 
  it is (obviously) only available as a shared storage interconnect...

	--

  When posting, please remember to include the OpenVMS version and the
  OpenVMS platform -- this can help us suggest alternatives, and to point 
  out platform- or version-specific features and/or considerations and/or
  options.  Thanks!

