Hmm - an interesting situation.  For the purposes of our license,
"free" means simply that  no compensation is made for use of the
software - not that the source is released to the public domain.  Do I
understand correctly that the NWP "code" is avaliable for anyone to
use at no cost? 

It is clear to me that the institutes themselves would NOT qualify for
the Enthusiast license, but it seems to me that independent
programmers helping to improve the code base would - the key phrase in
the current license wording is "Any work performed or produced as a
result of use of this Software cannot be performed or produced for the
benefit of other parties for a fee, compensation or any other
reimbursement or remuneration."

I've been asked to compile a list of "situations" so that we can go
over them and figure out what we want to allow and then make sure the
license wording says what we want.


