> that or not so the only way to find out was to go through the
> installation process and try!).  I guess I get to free up all that
> disk space!
>

This isn't quite true. StarOffice by default gives you a single
view on the desktop of the current document you are editing.

You can have multiple documents open and they appear on the
task bar along the bottom of the StarOffice window and you
can select which document to view by clicking the task bar.

However you can also specify that each task is a floating
task and then you get multiple overlapping windows each
with a text, graphic etc etc file in.

To try this open two or three documents, the documents you
have opened will appear as tasks on the task bar. Then use the
right button of your mouse (or what erver pointing device you
use ) to select the menu for each active task. Floating tasks
are an option on the menu.

If you do this you will find that you can have multiple overlapping
text windows.


