In 1979 rms believed in free passwords as well. All his accounts were
username rms with no password (or password rms if forced) and he
publicicsed this!

As I'm sure you recall DEC used to ship source code for TOPS-10, TOPS-
20 (not all sites) and all the associated layered products prior to
VMS. It was normal to see SPRs submitted with source code fixes. In
fact I still have somewhere an old response to a PA1050 SPR of mine
stating "your suggested  fix has been accepted verbatim"; which doesn't
sound quite so impressive when you realise it was a one line patch
(HRRZ replaced by MOVE) - but it was a clever one line patch :-).

So rms asking for the VMS sources to 'fix' doesn't sound so strange
when you consider that DEC had been doing just that with other OSs for
years. Many useful extensions to things such as SOS, EXEC, FILCOM, etc
all appeared because of this policy. The downside, of course, was that
you never had any idea how vanilla or otherwise any individual site was.

