concept seems to run counter to the exclusive access demanded by such
programs. Each "instance" would demand exclusive access to the file
being edited. I've never seen anything in M$-Word to allow a portion of
a document to be "opened" in a separate window. Then again, I'm hardly
the definitive power-user, either, when it comes to Micro$haft
WhineDoze.

