Try pressing the unload button 5 times in fairly rapid squence.

Search the news archives http://www.deja.com for TK50, TK70, and TZ30 for
more information, and tips.

The TZ30 is a CompacTape drive not a DLT, inspite of them having the same
form factor.  DLT tapes will not work in the unit, even if you manage to get
one in.

Use only CompacTape or CompacTape II cartridges in it, assuming that you can
salvage the drive.

If you must sacrifice the tape, (a high probability), then after you rehook
the leader, the drive may still function.

For your particular hardware, I would recommend looking for a used 4mm tape
drive.

TK50s only hold 95 Mb, and the tapes are no longer being sold.

