I disagree on the naming.  Both CompacTape I and II are still DLT tapes and
drives, just very early versions.  I think the TZ30 and TZ50 were both
15/30, or even 10/20 DLT drives.  Of course, at that time, the concept of
Digital linear tape still meant that Digital Equipment made and sold them.
Nowadays, the D in DLT is generic instead of referring to the manufacturer
of the drive...

CompacTape refers to the brand name of the tape manufacturer, which was
originally 3M.  Today's DLT drives (35/70) use 3M's CompacTape IV, I
believe...

