would do the same, if they could.  According to it's enemies, MS has been 'TOO'
successful.  Too bad there's never been a de facto standard of when a company
should reign in its success.

I'm not too happy about what MS has done to the world.  Basically, I see them
reducing what is expected from computers.  They can do this because there are a
lot more people who use 'typewriters' than forecast the weather.  The quantity
of their users basically eclipses all other uses of computers and reduces all of
