We shall see... I concluded my write-up (which my subscribers now have) with
the following:

Monday's Alpha announcement was less than earth-shattering, but the $500M
incremental investment and API's new status as an Alpha architectural
licensee are good news. Now it's time for the triumvirate to execute: as
long as the Alpha triumvirate can maintain Alpha's performance advantage
while reducing costs and improving marketing, SKC feels that a near-term
Omega for Alpha is an unlikely prospect indeed.

I took particular interest in the fact that Intel soon will cease to be a
factor in Alpha fabbing, and that the Q **finally** 'fessed up to the fact
that IBM will begin fabbing Alphas in the CMOS8/EV7 timeframe.

cheers,

