Hi,

I'm considering trying to upgrade my PWS with a faster processor, but
before I buy it, I would like to know if it is possible to install it of
course.

This is what I found out so far about the speed settings on these
systems:



		switch settings		system freq.	mult. factor
system		8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 

433 a/au	d u d u u d d u		61.9 MHz	7
500 a/au	d u u u u d d u		62,5 MHz	8
600 a/au	d d u d d u d u		66,7		9

d = down = on , u = up	

The multiplication factor was calculated by me from the system frequency
and the processor speed. Normally one would expect to see some
recognizable pattern in the switches, but I can't find any. For instance
7 would show up as 0111, 8 as 1000, and 9 as 1001, but no luck. 

Does anyone has a notion which logic is behind the swtch settings ??

The technical reference of these stations also mentions a 767 MHz board,
but I've never seen or heard of a 767 MHz 21164 yet.



Regards,

Dirk



