    Yes, it is a Turbochannel bus, probably 25MHz. What frame buffer is
this? A PMAG-JA? Chances are that the reason the card is not supported is
because no one at NetBSD has a card to write support for it. That being the
case, if you could lend someone at NetBSD a frame buffer, I'm sure they will
be more than happy to write support in for you. FYI: Most of the higher end
FB's have just become supported in -current (non-release), at least for the
MIPS DECstations. I haven't had the fortune of any dealing with Alpha's. I'm
stuck with a 5000/25 and a 5000/240 to try and learn C/C++ and some UNIX.
I'm sure the netbsd-pmax port maintainer could use one of the 5000/25's to
test/develop on if your willing to donate one also. As was mentioned, post
to port-pmax@netbsd.org for DECstation info, or port-alpha@netbsd.org for
Alpha. Hope that helps



