Folks,

At the following URL, you can find an update to the LD062 kit:
ftp://ftp.kgb.com/djesys/ld062.zip

The server space was graciously provided by Kevin G. Barkes of KGB
Consulting. I will be updating the link on my OpenVMS Freeware page to
reflect the new URL.

Here's the contents of the README.TXT file that was added to the
archive:

README.TXT File for Logical Disk V6.2 (LD062)                 
14-Dec-1999
==========================================================================

This version of the LD062.ZIP file was reprocessed by David J. Dachtera
of DJE Systems, Elmhurst, IL USA, djesys@earthlink.net.

As available from ftp.digital.com, the LD062.ZIP archive was not created
correctly: the /VMS qualifier was not used, nor was maximal compression
specified. This has been corrected. The content of the .ZIP archive is 
now the savesets plus this text file, instead of a single BACKUP
saveset.

As available from ftp.digital.com, the KITINSTAL.COM procedure in the 
.A saveset attempted to notify the author of LD (vdburg@mail.dec.com)
at the end of the install. This usually caused the installation to 
terminate abnormally. The associated DCL code was commented out.

LD062 remains unsupported freeware, (C)Digital Equipment Corp.

