On Mon, 08 Nov 1999 18:22:20 -0500, joe comunale <jbc@qcunix.qc.edu> wrote:
>I bought a DEC 64bit Alpha 166MHz Multia.  I will be getting Tru64 5.0
>very soon, and am now in (near desparate) need of a CD-ROM drive -
>internal, or external (although I would prefer to have an internal).
>What types will do?

You can't fit a CD-ROM drive inside a Multia.  If your Multia has an
external SCSI port, you can hook one up to that.  If not, and all
you're using it for is to install the OS, then you could attach an
internal drive that hangs out of the case, but you'll need a gender
changer for the SCSI cable (unless you're using an IDE drive) as the
cable hardwired to the SCSI board supports only one device.

-Scott



