You've already been given some good suggestions by others.  I will add another
potential source.  Get on WWW.EBAY.COM (when they're up), go to computers, and
do a search for DEC.  You'll periodically find DSP3105
and DSP3107 along with RZ26 (all 1 GB) disks that go for well under $50. You'll
also find 2.1 GB drives in the same price range.

Fairly rare, but if you're running V7.2 or higher, I really like the ST39173N
Seagate drives.  I've beat them fairly hard and no problems. They are the LP
Barracudas, and run much cooler than the earlier Barracudas.

With buying on EBAY you are taking risks.  My feeling is that for non-critical
use, the DSP3210 drives for under $50 is not much of a risk.  These are the DEC
OEM drives that were used for RZ28s before DEC sold the storage division to
Quantum.  Since Compaq is not replacing the drive under a maintenance contract
I'm guessing the usage is non-critical.

If this is for important data on a production system, Call Compaq and buy
approved drives with a 3-year warranty.  Any money saved elsewhere just isn't
worth any risk at all.  With critical data, how much can you afford to save?

Dave


