In article <o2254.1766$Dh3.49147@ozemail.com.au>, "Geoff Roberts" <geoffrob@stmarks.pp.catholic.edu.au> writes:
:
:Would some kind soul point me at where to find info on changing the drive id
:no on an RA90/92 SDI drive.

  From dim memory -- I usually end up poking the drive buttons until the 
  drive does what I want :-) -- try the following sequence:

    Dismount the drive from all cluster nodes...
    Spin down the RA90 or RA92 drive...
    Take both A and B ports offline...
    Push the test button...
    Port A button now selects the digit to change...
    Port B now changes the selected digit...
    255 is the maximum unit allowed (though IIRC SDI itself "allows" 4096)...
    Push the test button, the drive will then request confirmation...
    Press B if you really want to change the unit number...
    Press test again...
    Select the A, B, or both port(s) as needed, and spin up the drive...

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




