Chris Scheers wrote:
> 
> Are there any diagnostic lights for the AS255?  The LED labeled
> diagnostic appears to just come on at power up and then go off during
> the self tests.  I have not seen it flash.

There are lights on the motherboard.  I don't recall where they are.
I don't have a 255 here presently.

> Are there any more substantial diagnostics for this machine than the
> built in ones?  If so, where can I get them?

The firmware for the AlphaStation 200/400 series is much more limited than
the rest of the Alpha systems other workstations included.  Other systems
can do much more in the firmware but I doubt that what you're seeing would
be picked up.  It sounds like an intermittently flaky power supply or
motherboard.  I probably won't crap out while you're looking at it!

> Once the system has decided to switch to the serial console, how do you
> switch it back if you do not have a terminal handy?

I many cases you won't need to.  The console firmware will select a console
mode based on the availability of the console regardless of the console
firmware variable setting.  The console variable only takes precedence if
both consoles are available.  I think it's a bit like ewa0_mode for UTP and
BNC selection.  This variable (ewa0_mode) only selects which interface to
use if neither one or both of them are available.  In the case of the
console variable, if both are available the firmware needs to be able to
pick one.  If neither are available... Oh well :-)  I don't know if that's a
fatal condition or not.

> When DEC shipped this machine to us, no hardware manual was included.
> (It was rotational equipment.)  What is the order number for this
> manual?  Is it available online?

I don't recall if there was a publicly accessible one or not.  There was 
URL through DBL or ASAP that had it but I think it's gone.  I have PDFs of
manuals for the PWS but not the AS 255.  I do have a service guide that was
done as a Window help file that came from the DBL site.  I think it's OK for
me to mail it to you.  Let me know if you're interested.

> PS: I did find out something interesting during all this.  Once you get
> to the ">>>" prompt, the graphics head and both serial ports all work as
> console ports, irrespective of the console setting.  Are other Alphas
> like this?

Others that I've seen are.



