It's not uncommon in VMS clusters to have a drive with redundant
controllers.
Typically, a couple of HSC's would each have one port on a drive, so that if
the
HSC went down, the drive could still be accessed from the other one.
Combine this with drive shadowing and you have an excellent, redundant file
storage
system.  I believe there are speed of access benefits as well.

