In article <38555BAC.1BB047A2@calstatela.edu>, brian magness wrote:
>Hello Vax Users,
>I would like to know how one can copy files from a users directory to a
>tape drive(TK-50). I have recently acquired a microvax 3100-20 running
>VMS 5.3 and would like to copy files for storage. Is the command
>structure the same for a diskette drive(assuming I know the device
>name)Does the device have to be mounted first to copy files from the
>default users directory?

	You have a couple of possibilities -- BACKUP and COPY -- check them
out in HELP.  You'll need to INIT the tape first; for BACKUP you may need
to MOUNT/FOREIGN (ISTR that at some point BACKUP changed to not needing a
MOUNT), for COPY you will need to MOUNT.  You may need to use ALLOCATE and
DEALLOCATE, too.

