: I'm trying to help (VMS 6.2 VAX & Alpha) with different UCX versions,
: but (after changing your distributed files from stream-LF to just
: stream with FILE) my DEC C compiler (V5.2-003) says "virtual memory
: limits exceeded" on ckuu54 and ckcuni.
: 
: Can anyone tell me which quota(s) I need to up and to what?
: 
From Section VI of CKVINS.TXT:

Before trying to compile, make sure you've got the disk space and quotas, etc,
that are needed.  In version 6.0 and later, you'll probably need as much as 8
or 10 megabytes for all the sources, objects, and binaries.

The User Authorization File (UAF) parameters of the account in which C-Kermit
will be built must be set to accomodate the large size of some source modules.
Recommended values are:

  PAGE FILE QUOTA:  at least 60000
  Working set extent:  at least 5012

To modify: Suppose a user KERMIT is the VMS account from which Kermit is
maintained.  To set these values, the system manager must do the following:

  $ set default sys$system
  $ mcr authorize
  UAF> modify kermit/pgflquo=60000/wsextent=5012
  UAF> exit

If errors such as:

  %cc-f-text Virtual Memory limits exceeded

occur during the build procedure, these parameters may need adjustment
(upwards).

- Frank



