Hmmm, well, yes and no.  The code is written, enabled, and working for UNIX.
But it hasn't been ported to VMS.  The main hangup is all the time
functions.  Anybody who is familiar with gettimeofday(), localtime(), UNIX
time structs, and all that, and their VMS equivalents, is welcome to give it
a shot and then we'll have it in the final release for VMS too.  It should
be about 30 minutes work for somebody who knows what they're doing.

Another aspect is security.  As you might know, we have SSL/TLS in the UNIX
version, but not VMS.  Again, it's just an issue of porting the UNIX code
by a competent VMS programmer (i.e. not me).  When this works, then we have
secure HTTP GET, PUT, etc.

Ditto for Kerberos IV and V and SRP, though these don't bear directly on the
HTTP question.  I understand Compaq is now taking an interest in Kerberos
for VMS...

- Frank



