It's always better to have more binaries to choose from, because the number
of reasons any particular binary might not work are many: library mismatch,
Y2K patches, compiler bugs, etc... who knows what else.  The same is true in
the UNIX world with the increasing use of dll's, and the confusion with
libc/glibc, curses/ncurses, etc, especially when numbering systems are not
coordinated.  Ideally everybody would have C compilers and then we would not
have to make hundreds of binaries, but that's a dream world.

The other problem is that UCX is actually somewhat hard to find.  I have it
here but only for two builds (VAX/VMS 5.5-2 + UCX 2.0, and Alpha VMS 7.1 +
UCX 4-point-something).  Most sites have Multinet.

Again, my plea for volunteers to make builds that I or other current
volunteers can't make: Anything earlier than VMS 4.7; anything between VMS
5.0 and 5.4 (inclusive); VMS 6-point-anything on VAX, VMS 7.2 on VAX, etc
etc, with or without any or all networking products.  The current list is at
the bottom of:

  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ck70.html

Upload them to:

  ftp://kermit.columbia.edu/kermit/incoming/

using the same naming conventions.  (Or if you want me to do the builds
myself, I'll be glad to -- just send e-mail to arrange it.)

Thanks!

- Frank



