My AS255 just threw me a scare.  It suddenly disappeared from the
network.  When I went to check, it had a message something like:

	KEYBOARD ERROR: Switched to serial console.

Since I wasn't watching it at the time, I don't know if it reset and
went through self test or not, but I assume it did.

I replaced the keyboard and powered it back on.  Got the same message.

I then cycled power again and got nothing.  The hard disk didn't even
spin up.  I tried this a few times and didn't get anthing on the
display.  The lights on the keyboard would flash when power was applied,
but that was all.  The two lights on the front of the machine were both
on.  The diagnostic LED on the motherboard came on with power and never
flashed.

I turned the machine off while I went to hunt up a terminal.  It was off
for about 20 minutes, perhaps long enough for something to cool down. 
(The CPU fan is functioning.)

When I booted with the terminal attached, the system worked.  In fact,
the system had switched back to using the graphics head as the console.

Everything is now working, including the original keyboard.

Has anyone seen anything like this before?  Any suggestions as to what
the problem might be?  (I have checked the voltages on the power supply
and they are correct.  I have not checked for ripple.)

Are there any diagnostic lights for the AS255?  The LED labeled
diagnostic appears to just come on at power up and then go off during
the self tests.  I have not seen it flash.

Are there any more substantial diagnostics for this machine than the
built in ones?  If so, where can I get them?

Once the system has decided to switch to the serial console, how do you
switch it back if you do not have a terminal handy?

When DEC shipped this machine to us, no hardware manual was included. 
(It was rotational equipment.)  What is the order number for this
manual?  Is it available online?

Thanx!


PS: I did find out something interesting during all this.  Once you get
to the ">>>" prompt, the graphics head and both serial ports all work as
console ports, irrespective of the console setting.  Are other Alphas
like this?

