> I have an alpha-based 21264 workstation which is complaining of 'too
> many users' when there are four people logged on. The kernel is
> configured for a maximum of 64 (overkill, I know!). My Digital Unix 4.0e
> licenses make no mention of user limits, but knowing Digital I suspect
> that it is nevertheless a license problem.
> 
> Before I tell the boss that we need to spend yet more money, is there
> something obvious I have missed?

You can see the loaded licences with a "lmf list full".

>Other things to look for, allthough they give another error message is :

THe above error messages looks like a license related thing, but :

Device files in /dev
In 4.0e I think there are 32 by default on AlphaServers (I don't know if
it's different on AlphaWorkstations), so if you have more users than
device files you'll run into a problem.
It's written in the manual somewhere how to make more of these files, I
think a cd to /dev and a "./MAKEDEV PTY_1" should make a few. Exchange 1
with 2,3,4,5,6,7,8 and 9 to get more.
The device files is linked with the pts sysconfigtab parameter. It's 255
as default on AlphaServers. A "sysconfig -q pts" will tell you what it
is. If you need to change it (it should be at least the same as the
number of pty device files), put something like this in
/etc/sysconfigtab :

pts:
	nptys = 1024



l8r/Jspr



