"Simon Maslin" <Simon.Maslin@dlr.de> writes:

> How exactly does the msync() call actually synchronise the cluster-wide
> applications that are mapped to the disk file ?

AFAIK, you can't do that across cluster members. Presumably, msync() writes
all modified pages to the section file, and maps to the $UPDSEC system call.
However, there is no way, short of unmapping and remapping the section file,
that the other node can invalidate its local copy of those modified pages so
that they will be read from disk the next time they are accessed.

Describe in more detail the problem you want to solve, if you want help.

	Jan



