Sounds like you've got an IDE disk there.

FWIW, I had that problem with a DECpc 450-ST with two RZ25s (SCSI
disks). It wouldn't successfully boot from the hard disk until I did
this:

A:\>FDISK/MBR

This seemed to fix the problem. The machine previously had SCO UNIX
installed on it, so I had to reformat the disks.

Don't know if it'll work for you, but wanted to suggest it.

