    from the remaining members of the Raidset. It doesn't appear
    to have done this. I suppose I could have forced this by
    failing the entire drive out of the set, but that seems
    rather drastic. Does the controller only use the redundant
    drive information if a disk fails entirely and not if
    only certain blocks can't be read correctly?

