In article <3846FFF6.8D9E8F07@dont.spam>, 
        "William R. Frenchu" <please@dont.spam> writes:
> 
> I was recently given a couple of Digital mice, part number V8XXX-AA.C03.
                                                              ^
        I think you'll find, on closer inspection, that the part number
    is VSXXX-AA.
        ^

> There's no little roller ball in this one, though, just two "buttons"
> on the underside. Is this some kind of "optical" mouse?

        That mouse is a variation on the "hockey-puck" style DEC mouse.
    The exterior surface (bottom) of each  "button" is beveled so that
    the point of contact with the desk (or mouse pad) is off axis.  The
    buttons rotate about an axis perpendicular to the bottom of the
    mouse, and, IIRC, one is for X and the other for Y movements.

>                                                         If so, what
