>I was recently given a couple of Digital mice, part number V8XXX-AA.C03.
>There's no little roller ball in this one, though, just two "buttons"
>on the underside. Is this some kind of "optical" mouse? If so, what
>sort of mouse pad is necessary to use it? Would it be (with the
>appropriate mouse pad) compatible with my Vaxstation 3100?

Is it 'VSXXX', rather than 'V8XXX'?

If you look closely, you'll see that the two 'buttons' are angled
slightly, such that they make contact with the desk surface and
roll when the mouse is moved.  One roller is for the X-axis and
the other for the Y-axis.  It's a nice mouse design.  Gunge doesn't
get inside and build up on rollers like in standard mice.

You don't need a special mouse pad.  I can be absolutely sure about
compatibility with the VS3100, but if the connector fits, you should 
be OK.  I had no trouble using a V8XXX-AA.C03 on a DECstation and
a VAXstation 3500.

