shsrms/aka/shsrms wrote:
> 
> This has been a great turn of events on this thread!
> Now, bold face and bald face both have been used interchangably in my
> circles.
> What is the derivation of the phrases?
> I always detected a slight idiomatic difference, but could have been
> my imaginings.
> Bold face being an out right lie, and bald face being a naive statement.

Interesting observation. I must admit - the subtlety had escaped me.
Yes, that is quite an interesting distinction! "Bold", in a negative
context, implying intentional or flagrant deceit, and "bald" (ant.
"hirsute") implying youth (syn. "naive" or "callow", "inexperienced").

