                                    Tru64 Unix Developer's Survey

Compaq would like to learn about the tools that developers are using (and
would like to use) to develop applications for Tru64 Unix to drive the
direction of future products. Compaq would appreciate your input on the
following survey. Just cut and paste the following questions into your
favorite email client and send it along to alpha-developer@compaq.com. Your
answers will give us some very important information and insight into future
product planning.

1. Which of the following best describes the applications you develop for
Tru64 Unix
? Commercial/ISV
? Academic
? Hobbiest/OpenSource/FreeWare/ShareWare
? Commercial, proprietary "inhouse" applications

2. Which languages do you use in your application development?
? C
? C++
? FORTRAN
? COBOL
? PASCAL
? Java
? Other (please specify)

3. Do you use Compaq compilers, third party compilers or open source
compilers such as gcc/egcs?

If you use Compaq Compilers, tell us your likes and dislikes about them

If you use open source compilers, tell us why (i.e. cost, compatibility,
etc)


4. What other development tools do you use (debuggers, profilers, etc) from
either Compaq or third party independent software vendors?

5. Are there any development tools which you use on other platforms which
you would like to see made available for Tru64 Unix?

6. Please give us any general comments you may have about the Tru64 Unix
development environment.

7. Is your company a member of the Compaq Solutions Alliance? (Yes/No)
    If not and would like information on joining, more information about the
program can be found at
    http://www.compaq.com/csa







