: 
You will need a Kermit program on each computer, preferably C-Kermit:

  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ckermit.html

Then if you have enough space of the 750, use VMS ZIP to make a VMS-format
ZIP archive, and then transfer it with Kermit.

If you don't have ZIP, you can also use a BACKUP saveset for this.

Assuming you have C-Kermit 6.0 or later on each computer, it will transfer
the ZIP file or BACKUP saveset correctly.  This is all explained in the VMS
Appendix of the manual.

- Frank





